  "title": "Shared-space service robot · Level 2: Clear a table while people cross",
  "brief": "As level 1, while two people (400 mm across) walk across the hall between the tables, each on its own line, at 200 mm/s from a seeded place and direction: they stop rather than walk into your robot. Never touch a person, and never pass within 200 mm of one (measured from any part of your robot, the scoop's tip included) while moving faster than 100 mm/s: a run that does scores 0, and one such run fails the level. Your robot is the hall carrier with two more distance sensors turned 30° to each side (I2C 7 right, I2C 9 left), as in G6.4.5's Deepen, mounted 60 mm up like its front one (so they look over a cup). Shut the door, collect the cup at table 3's pickup point, return it to the blue station. The run ends when your program ends (and the robot stands still), or at 120 s. 60 for the tray returned, plus 40 × min(1, par ÷ time) when it is. Pass: mean 60 or more, the cup delivered in at least 4 of 5 runs, and no run breaks the safety gate.",
